<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laguna (province)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laguna is a province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luzon">Luzon</a>, south-east of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a>, lying along the southern shore of the lake <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/laguna-de-bay">Laguna de Bay</a>. It was a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-revolution">Philippine Revolution</a> and of resistance in the Philippine-American War. The national hero <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-rizal">José Rizal</a> was born in its town of Calamba.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/laguna-province.jpg" alt="Laguna (province)" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ralff Nestor Nacor · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Laguna_Provincial_Capitol,_Dec_2023_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
